WEBVTT

00:45.128 --> 00:47.213
- Oh, wait for me.
- Oh.

00:58.475 --> 00:59.809
Doors closing.

00:59.893 --> 01:01.269
Hold the door, please.

01:01.352 --> 01:02.854
Doors opening.

01:02.937 --> 01:04.064
Ah.

01:04.689 --> 01:06.399
Heading home?

01:07.442 --> 01:08.693
Doors closing.

01:13.823 --> 01:14.991
What did you get?

01:17.285 --> 01:18.787
A new faucet for the kitchen.

01:18.870 --> 01:21.206
- Mine's leaking.
- Oh.

01:21.289 --> 01:22.707
Wouldn't the landlord…

01:23.958 --> 01:26.628
Oh, hang on. You own it, don't you?

01:26.711 --> 01:29.130
Wow, that's great.

01:29.214 --> 01:31.091
Technically, it belongs to the bank.

01:31.174 --> 01:33.051
Still, if it's in your name,
that's awesome.

01:33.134 --> 01:35.595
Good for you.

01:35.678 --> 01:37.889
You got a great job and a great place.

01:37.972 --> 01:39.516
Whoever she is, she's lucky.

01:40.058 --> 01:42.936
- Who?
- Whoever you marry one day.

01:49.192 --> 01:51.528
Twelfth floor. Doors opening.

01:52.445 --> 01:54.239
- That's me.
- See ya. Bye.

01:59.035 --> 02:01.037
Doors closing.

02:01.663 --> 02:02.831
Who are you?

02:04.374 --> 02:06.376
Hm? Is there something
I can help you with?

02:07.001 --> 02:08.378
You don't…

02:08.461 --> 02:09.879
My daughter lives here.

02:14.217 --> 02:16.094
- Uh…
- Oh?

02:26.020 --> 02:27.188
Good evening.

02:29.774 --> 02:30.942
Hello.

02:45.540 --> 02:47.250
Say you will.

02:47.333 --> 02:50.253
Say you will.

02:54.299 --> 02:55.717
Why would they take a risk like that?

02:55.800 --> 02:59.137
That whole thing
of marriage being the end goal,

02:59.220 --> 03:00.430
it's not always right.

03:06.769 --> 03:09.731
LEE SI-WOO

03:13.318 --> 03:14.235
Hey, I just finished--

03:14.319 --> 03:16.696
I think you should go home
right away.

03:17.572 --> 03:18.489
Huh?

03:21.701 --> 03:24.495
To summarize and make sure I understand,

03:25.747 --> 03:27.957
all of you are living together,
because of your work?

03:28.041 --> 03:29.959
Yes. We work together. So that's why.

03:30.460 --> 03:31.753
When will you go?

03:31.836 --> 03:33.671
Uh, we'll leave…

03:34.255 --> 03:36.507
When we can go to our houses--

03:36.591 --> 03:39.219
No, just until the season's over.

03:39.302 --> 03:40.511
That's right, yeah.

03:41.763 --> 03:43.848
You'll be here the rest of the season.

03:45.225 --> 03:46.684
Several months away.

03:46.768 --> 03:48.311
- Yes.
- Yeah.

03:49.938 --> 03:51.648
She's gone crazy letting not just one

03:51.731 --> 03:54.275
but two men live in her apartment
when she lives alone?

03:54.901 --> 03:58.321
Oh, the weather this time of year
is especially dangerous.

03:58.404 --> 04:01.407
And just makes sense to be able to review
and discuss it at any time, right?

04:01.491 --> 04:03.451
Yes. Yeah, it makes sense.

04:04.577 --> 04:06.913
I apologize if we alarmed you
at all, madam.

04:08.331 --> 04:09.540
Right. Okay.

04:09.624 --> 04:12.627
My daughter isn't going to be
a perky spring chicken forever,

04:12.710 --> 04:15.755
so I'm worried she must've lost her mind.

04:17.966 --> 04:19.300
What's a spring chicken?

04:20.134 --> 04:21.886
Someone who can get a husband easily.

04:22.762 --> 04:24.389
Also, I was wondering about,

04:24.472 --> 04:27.225
in the elevator,
there was a man you were talking to.

04:27.308 --> 04:29.185
How exactly does he know you?

04:29.769 --> 04:31.771
Oh, he works with us at the KMA.

04:32.272 --> 04:33.439
- Who?
- Seok-ho.

04:33.523 --> 04:35.275
Oh, of course. Seok-ho's on team two.

04:35.358 --> 04:37.360
Oh, and is he spoken for?

04:37.443 --> 04:38.945
- Oh, no, not yet.
- Yes, he's single.

04:39.028 --> 04:41.030
- His age?
- Huh?

04:41.114 --> 04:44.033
I wanna know how old that man,
your co-worker is.

04:44.117 --> 04:46.953
I think he's the same age
as Miss Jin, isn't he?

04:47.036 --> 04:48.997
- Oh.
- He's not…

04:49.080 --> 04:51.374
Uh, Seok-ho is a few years older
than he looks.

04:51.457 --> 04:54.419
So he'd actually be older than Miss Jin.

04:55.795 --> 04:57.130
Uh, seven years older.

04:57.213 --> 04:58.798
Oh.

05:00.883 --> 05:04.387
Seven years? That'd be okay.

05:05.805 --> 05:07.432
Seven years?

05:11.102 --> 05:13.730
Mom, you should've told me
you were coming.

05:13.813 --> 05:16.524
How could you let these random men
into your home?

05:16.607 --> 05:18.943
You should've at least discussed it
with me first.

05:19.527 --> 05:20.737
Please. I know who they are.

05:20.820 --> 05:23.114
It's just Mr. Um
and a forecaster from team two.

05:24.574 --> 05:26.242
I knew things were off

05:26.326 --> 05:29.370
when you hurried over after I threatened
to come here and get you.

05:29.996 --> 05:32.248
I thought there must be some secret here
you've been hiding.

05:32.915 --> 05:34.208
And I…

05:35.043 --> 05:36.586
It's just because of work.

05:36.669 --> 05:38.379
It's our busiest season
and I'm overwhelmed,

05:38.463 --> 05:39.922
because I've never done this
as a director.

05:40.006 --> 05:42.091
There's a lot on my plate,
so they're helping me out.

05:42.175 --> 05:43.259
Yeah, right.

05:43.760 --> 05:46.596
When did you start asking for help
when you're overwhelmed?

05:46.679 --> 05:49.140
You'd suffer in silence
until it killed you, I know.

05:50.350 --> 05:52.769
Let's not do this here. Follow me.

05:52.852 --> 05:54.520
It's too hot. Let's talk here.

05:54.604 --> 05:56.606
- Come on, we need to go. Mom!
- Huh?

05:57.815 --> 05:58.858
Ridiculous.

05:58.941 --> 06:00.735
- See you…
- Good night, ma'am.

06:24.175 --> 06:26.427
MOM

06:34.060 --> 06:35.311
Hey, Mom.

06:36.396 --> 06:37.897
Ugh, I know.

06:37.980 --> 06:41.192
Work came up and I had no choice,
I couldn't get away.

06:42.151 --> 06:44.529
Sorry, we'll do a belated birthday.

06:45.696 --> 06:47.198
Hm? A bag?

06:52.453 --> 06:54.372
- Did you go shopping again?
- Oh, that's--

06:54.455 --> 06:55.998
Must be nice to be so carefree.

06:56.082 --> 07:00.002
Are you saying that I'm just
thoughtlessly spending our money?

07:01.087 --> 07:02.171
If you're being rational,

07:02.880 --> 07:05.341
you wouldn't spend our money
like it's nothing.

07:09.220 --> 07:10.430
Oh, uh…

07:11.264 --> 07:12.974
Right. How did I forget it?

07:13.808 --> 07:16.436
Actually, Yu-jin picked
the bag out for you, yeah.

07:17.061 --> 07:18.688
I told you before.

07:18.771 --> 07:21.023
Yu-jin's great. She's really thoughtful.

07:21.107 --> 07:24.277
You always say she's no Ha-kyung,
like I made a mistake,

07:24.360 --> 07:26.487
but you'll see, she's wonderful.

07:30.741 --> 07:32.702
Mm. Is that so?

07:32.785 --> 07:35.371
Why don't you give her a call
and grab dinner again sometime?

07:36.080 --> 07:37.206
Mm.

07:38.583 --> 07:39.750
Mm-hm.

07:44.464 --> 07:48.259
Oh, no. Damn it. I'm such an idiot.

08:23.085 --> 08:27.048
Um… Uh…

08:27.131 --> 08:30.510
You could've… You should've told me.

08:33.262 --> 08:34.514
About the purse.

08:36.849 --> 08:39.227
She took it when she went
to meet her friend,

08:39.310 --> 08:40.853
and everyone noticed it.

08:40.937 --> 08:43.314
She called and told me all about it.

08:43.397 --> 08:45.650
They all said she's lucky to have
a great daughter-in-law.

08:45.733 --> 08:46.734
It was a real compliment.

08:48.402 --> 08:50.154
I'm sorry for what I said

08:50.988 --> 08:51.906
the other day.

08:54.200 --> 08:55.284
Well, now you know.

08:57.453 --> 08:58.579
Also,

08:59.622 --> 09:01.290
how did you pay for the bag?

09:01.916 --> 09:04.919
We're maxed out on all our credit cards.

09:05.002 --> 09:08.005
I used my bonus,
plus a little from my emergency fund.

09:09.924 --> 09:12.927
We're so busy right now,
we don't even have time

09:13.010 --> 09:14.220
to dream about a vacation.

09:15.471 --> 09:18.224
It seemed like a better idea to use it
for the gift.

09:21.060 --> 09:22.436
Thanks for that, Yu-jin.

09:23.729 --> 09:26.482
I haven't been thinking straight
the past few days.

09:28.234 --> 09:29.402
Whatever.

09:29.485 --> 09:31.988
Oh, forgive me just this once.

09:38.327 --> 09:40.288
I'm the worst. Please forgive me.

09:40.371 --> 09:42.707
You want a massage?

09:45.459 --> 09:47.253
I'm so sorry. I'll be better.

09:49.005 --> 09:50.590
With more people living in the apartment,

09:50.673 --> 09:53.009
the water bills and electricity bills
are going to be higher.

09:53.092 --> 09:54.802
Are they gonna be covering the difference?

09:54.885 --> 09:56.304
They're staying as my guests.

09:56.387 --> 09:57.513
Huh.

09:58.264 --> 10:01.142
You should still split it with them,
plus maintenance.

10:01.726 --> 10:03.269
Mom, I'm their boss.

10:03.352 --> 10:04.895
Yeah, so?

10:06.856 --> 10:09.317
You're so smart and so clueless
at the same time.

10:12.236 --> 10:14.572
It seems like Director Jin's mom

10:16.032 --> 10:18.951
was really interested in Mr. Shin's life.

10:19.035 --> 10:21.245
Well, it doesn't even matter.
Ha-kyung doesn't see it that way.

10:21.329 --> 10:24.040
Her mom would set her up
with anyone she can find.

10:24.957 --> 10:28.586
Seok-ho is a little boring, isn't he?

10:28.669 --> 10:31.922
It's not like he's a perfect person,
I mean, no one is,

10:32.006 --> 10:35.468
but he seems difficult to live with too.

10:36.093 --> 10:38.888
He'd probably be a good husband,
though, wouldn't he?

10:41.682 --> 10:45.061
Well, even if he was, there's no way
he could ever date Ha-kyung.

10:46.062 --> 10:48.439
Seok-ho's not even… He and Director Jin,

10:48.939 --> 10:51.025
I think they're way too different
to be together.

10:51.609 --> 10:53.402
Different hobbies,
different personalities…

10:53.486 --> 10:55.821
And the chemistry is non-existent.
They don't have any.

10:55.905 --> 10:57.531
Hey.

10:58.699 --> 11:01.494
Stranger things have happened, you know?

11:01.577 --> 11:05.498
Romance is completely unpredictable,
you'll never know what will happen.

11:05.581 --> 11:07.667
Especially if they're working together
every day.

11:08.209 --> 11:09.210
Hey.

11:09.710 --> 11:14.173
You never know. Just you wait.

11:35.778 --> 11:36.862
So,

11:37.446 --> 11:40.991
the fellow that lives above you
works for the KMA?

11:41.617 --> 11:44.036
- The Assistant Director?
- He's what?

11:45.329 --> 11:49.041
I was thinking he seems really nice.
He seems nice and takes care of himself.

11:49.125 --> 11:50.751
- Right?
- Okay, and?

11:50.835 --> 11:52.545
- It's here.
- Well, he…

11:52.628 --> 11:55.089
He seems like he'd be great for you.

11:55.172 --> 11:57.508
And I want you to consider him,
just for a second.

11:57.591 --> 11:59.510
You could get to know him outside of work.

11:59.593 --> 12:01.762
I mean, who knows, huh? Consider it.

12:01.846 --> 12:03.764
Thank you. Get home safe, huh?

12:08.060 --> 12:10.020
He's the Assistant Director?

12:11.647 --> 12:13.649
Seven years isn't that bad.

12:33.043 --> 12:34.962
Did you get your mom a cab?

12:36.630 --> 12:37.673
Mm-hm.

12:40.801 --> 12:42.136
Si-woo, oppa…

12:42.845 --> 12:43.929
doesn't want marriage.

12:46.265 --> 12:50.019
He has no intention of marrying anyone.

12:53.647 --> 12:57.777
Ha-kyung doesn't date just anybody,
unless there's a chance of marriage.

13:00.237 --> 13:02.031
You are aware of that, right?

13:08.454 --> 13:10.873
- Maybe we should get… a drink?
- You want a beer?

13:14.460 --> 13:16.045
- Let's do it.
- Okay.

13:28.891 --> 13:30.976
So I was chatting with Miss Chae.

13:32.770 --> 13:34.939
And she said you don't believe
in marriage.

13:37.066 --> 13:37.900
Yeah.

13:44.824 --> 13:46.575
Would you mind explaining that more?

13:47.409 --> 13:49.370
It's just not something I'd ever want.

13:50.079 --> 13:53.415
I don't really think that you have
to get married to prove you're in love.

13:56.126 --> 13:58.629
And then you're responsible
for your in-laws,

13:58.712 --> 14:00.172
you owe everyone more.

14:01.340 --> 14:04.510
And I wouldn't want to weigh down
the person I love

14:05.928 --> 14:07.304
with my problems.

14:13.978 --> 14:17.314
So you think a larger family
has to be a burden?

14:17.898 --> 14:19.191
You've met my father.

14:22.528 --> 14:26.198
It just seems easiest to decide
I'll never do it.

14:32.371 --> 14:33.414
You're mad, aren't you?

14:34.123 --> 14:35.291
Uh, no.

14:36.625 --> 14:38.085
It's just that…

14:38.168 --> 14:40.713
I hadn't considered it, really, until now.

14:40.796 --> 14:43.090
Not getting married after dating.

14:44.508 --> 14:45.759
I want to say

14:45.843 --> 14:48.262
I don't want you to misunderstand
what I think of you.

14:48.888 --> 14:51.849
Not wanting to get married doesn't mean
I'm any less serious about us.

14:51.932 --> 14:54.226
- I'm not trying to lead you on.
- I know.

14:58.606 --> 14:59.648
I'm thinking about…

15:01.483 --> 15:04.945
what would we do when we're that serious?

15:07.573 --> 15:09.491
If you don't wind up getting married,

15:10.451 --> 15:14.371
how do you know when you've reached
the height of your love?

15:18.417 --> 15:21.211
Sleep is heavily affected
by temperature.

15:22.087 --> 15:23.130
When the weather is warm,

15:23.923 --> 15:26.175
our central nervous systems
are stimulated,

15:26.800 --> 15:28.594
and we have trouble falling asleep.

15:43.359 --> 15:46.278
A blizzard of thoughts
swirls in my head these nights.

15:48.155 --> 15:49.657
When I have too many thoughts at once,

15:50.157 --> 15:52.242
my heart gets confused.

15:52.326 --> 15:55.371
And a confused heart can only bring more

15:56.455 --> 15:59.375
and more and more thoughts.

16:02.836 --> 16:03.963
Too hot.

16:04.046 --> 16:06.590
Ugh. It's so hot.

16:07.466 --> 16:12.846
EPISODE 10
TROPICAL NIGHT

16:13.430 --> 16:17.351
The temperature last night
hit a low at just over 25 in Seoul.

16:17.434 --> 16:20.521
We had our first tropical night
of the season and of the year.

16:20.604 --> 16:22.690
It's really hot this morning as well…

16:22.773 --> 16:23.816
- Good morning.
- The temperatures will rise

16:23.899 --> 16:27.027
to exceed 31 degrees
during the day in many areas.

16:27.111 --> 16:30.322
- Ugh. Today's gonna be a rough one.
- I know. This is why

16:30.406 --> 16:33.492
I was hoping for rain,
cool the heat down a little.

16:35.160 --> 16:37.037
Humidity is high, too.

16:37.121 --> 16:38.789
So, of course, we've got heat.

16:41.375 --> 16:44.336
Why are you worried? Your face.

16:44.420 --> 16:45.963
Did you sleep all right?

16:46.046 --> 16:47.464
Oh, I just got too hot.

16:50.884 --> 16:52.553
We're probably making it worse.

16:52.636 --> 16:54.888
'Cause you have to have your door closed.

16:54.972 --> 16:56.932
Thankfully, I don't like
to keep the door open

16:57.016 --> 16:58.767
even when I'm alone and it's hot.

16:58.851 --> 17:00.227
So don't worry.

17:01.979 --> 17:03.105
I'm sorry, still.

17:03.772 --> 17:06.692
I'll go back home whenever I can.

17:06.775 --> 17:08.527
Well, no pressure for now.

17:15.325 --> 17:17.828
Oh. Look at him.

17:17.911 --> 17:19.788
You didn't sleep, either, did you?

17:20.372 --> 17:21.206
Why?

17:21.790 --> 17:24.084
It'll stay warm for a while now.

17:24.168 --> 17:26.253
It won't be fun.

17:26.962 --> 17:29.006
Hey, can I shower first?

17:29.089 --> 17:30.132
Okay.

17:39.767 --> 17:41.226
You didn't sleep well?

17:41.310 --> 17:42.770
It was too hot.

17:45.314 --> 17:46.315
Yeah. It was.

17:51.528 --> 17:53.530
Um…

17:55.032 --> 17:58.035
Everyone, you've all been
waiting for this for so long.

17:58.118 --> 18:01.163
What I have here
is the big three must-haves for newlyweds.

18:01.246 --> 18:03.165
Warm weather is here,
so we have an air conditioner,

18:03.248 --> 18:04.875
a refrigerator, and a washing machine--

18:04.958 --> 18:06.293
- Let's turn on the news.
- Yeah.

18:06.376 --> 18:10.130
…analyzing last year's total death
and birth rate, compared to marriage rate,

18:10.214 --> 18:11.965
we can plainly see that the date--

18:12.049 --> 18:14.176
- Coffee sounds good, no?
- Oh, and I can make some toast.

18:14.259 --> 18:15.385
- Sure.
- Okay.

18:20.140 --> 18:21.725
Doors opening.

18:29.608 --> 18:32.569
Stranger things have happened, you know?

18:32.653 --> 18:36.615
Romance is completely unpredictable,
you'll never know what will happen.

18:36.698 --> 18:39.243
Especially if they're working together
every day.

18:39.326 --> 18:40.452
Hey.

18:40.536 --> 18:42.579
You never know.

18:44.498 --> 18:46.208
- Oh, hey, did you have breakfast?
- Mm.

18:51.755 --> 18:53.799
Doors closing.

18:56.385 --> 18:59.763
Are you really making kimchi today?

18:59.847 --> 19:02.558
Hey, Ma, do you really need all that?

19:02.641 --> 19:05.394
Making moist young radish kimchi
with cold noodles is nutritious

19:05.477 --> 19:07.020
- and it's delicious.
- Yeah, I know that.

19:07.104 --> 19:09.523
But all this is gonna make
an insane amount.

19:09.606 --> 19:11.275
I might have a plan.

19:11.358 --> 19:13.652
- Here. Thank you.
- Thanks. Have a good day.

19:13.735 --> 19:14.945
Come on, there isn't much time.

19:15.028 --> 19:17.948
I've gotta get cooking. This kimchi needs
to be ready by the end of today.

19:19.575 --> 19:22.661
A plan? What are you doing?
When you say you have a plan,

19:22.744 --> 19:25.497
I start to get scared,
you'll make Ha-kyung mad.

19:27.416 --> 19:28.750
The…

19:29.918 --> 19:33.172
handsome guy, he lives above her.
My plan is to get him.

19:33.255 --> 19:35.841
- Huh?
- That guy.

19:35.924 --> 19:39.720
The guy. The guy who kept the food
for so long that you gave Ha-kyung.

19:39.803 --> 19:40.929
Oh, in 1302?

19:41.013 --> 19:44.349
Guess what? Ha-kyung said
he's on her team at work.

19:44.433 --> 19:45.267
Really?

19:46.059 --> 19:47.728
Why didn't he say that
when I talked to him?

19:47.811 --> 19:48.896
Huh?

19:49.479 --> 19:51.607
- You have talked?
- I… I don't know.

19:51.690 --> 19:54.193
We ran into each other once or twice.

19:54.693 --> 19:56.570
I think he might be a nice guy.

19:57.154 --> 20:00.115
No, no, no. You're setting her up
with another stranger.

20:00.199 --> 20:03.952
Exactly, yes, and you can help
if you talk again.

20:04.578 --> 20:07.039
- What?
- Don't play dumb.

20:07.122 --> 20:10.250
You have to do reconnaissance
to see if he's actually good enough.

20:10.334 --> 20:12.711
And if he is, then I'll make a suggestion.

20:13.337 --> 20:15.881
- Huh?
- Wow.

20:19.426 --> 20:21.970
I have a question
about the aerological data from Seoul…

20:24.848 --> 20:28.143
CHIEF TEAM TWO, DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

20:33.982 --> 20:35.901
Mrs. Oh.

20:36.944 --> 20:40.489
- Come on. Mrs. Oh!
- Huh? What?

20:41.782 --> 20:44.034
Here. Look at the AWS numbers in Taebaek.

20:44.117 --> 20:45.661
Does that look right?

20:45.744 --> 20:47.621
Yes, why?

20:51.458 --> 20:52.876
You seem tired. Are you okay?

20:52.960 --> 20:55.295
Oh, way too hot to sleep.

20:55.379 --> 20:58.090
Oh, our youngest couldn't sleep all night,

20:58.173 --> 21:00.842
so I had to stay up, too.

21:00.926 --> 21:02.678
I guess it's showing.

21:02.761 --> 21:04.763
We can't have the AC on, either.

21:05.931 --> 21:07.057
Couldn't your husband help?

21:07.140 --> 21:09.685
He has to focus on studying.

21:10.352 --> 21:12.229
Since we're committed for a year,

21:12.312 --> 21:15.065
I said to go all-in,
so he'll have no regrets.

21:16.108 --> 21:17.734
Well, it's so bad.

21:17.818 --> 21:19.945
I'm gonna splash some water on my face.

21:21.196 --> 21:22.281
Oh!

21:26.076 --> 21:28.704
It'd be faster for her to take the exam,
she'd get promoted.

21:30.831 --> 21:34.543
She had scored all the other Level Sevens
when she first came to KMA, you know?

21:34.626 --> 21:36.795
Perfectionist and focused,
she's lightning-fast,

21:36.878 --> 21:37.921
and has good leadership, too.

21:38.588 --> 21:41.550
So everyone thought
she'd be the next director.

21:42.050 --> 21:44.219
But she got married, had kids, and then…

21:44.303 --> 21:45.679
She couldn't do it all, anymore.

21:45.762 --> 21:48.181
I think that's why she's been stuck
for so long.

21:48.265 --> 21:51.727
And she has to take care
of her husband now with everything else.

21:51.810 --> 21:53.186
It must be hard.

21:53.770 --> 21:56.106
Good for her,
I couldn't last a day in her shoes.

21:56.189 --> 21:57.149
Could you?

21:57.733 --> 22:00.068
You can when it's for your kids.

22:00.152 --> 22:02.446
Mm. You're right.

22:04.072 --> 22:06.450
Did you… Did you not sleep too, director?

22:07.075 --> 22:09.119
Oh, the heat got to me.

22:09.202 --> 22:11.496
- Good talk.
- Huh.

22:13.248 --> 22:15.959
We should be exempt from weather
since we work here.

22:20.630 --> 22:24.343
- Hey, Chae Yu-jin.
- Huh? Is that…

22:24.885 --> 22:26.511
They let a city gangster in here?

22:26.595 --> 22:30.307
I guess that's what happens
when there's no drama in the city.

22:31.433 --> 22:33.060
So you thought you could find
a story here?

22:33.143 --> 22:34.853
You know what they say.

22:34.936 --> 22:37.481
"The KMA will save you
when there's nothing going on."

22:37.564 --> 22:40.025
If I hang around here,
something will turn up, you know?

22:41.151 --> 22:42.527
Also, uh…

22:42.611 --> 22:43.987
Is the food any good in this place?

22:44.738 --> 22:45.614
It's good.

22:45.697 --> 22:47.240
Okay. See you around.

22:56.291 --> 22:57.125
What's going on?

22:57.209 --> 22:59.211
I heard Heo Ju-yeong is at the KMA.

23:03.256 --> 23:06.009
- What? How did you hear?
- Ugh. No need to know that.

23:06.093 --> 23:09.221
Don't think about coming back
if that bastard steals your story.

23:09.763 --> 23:11.932
There's nothing to steal.
I don't have a story.

23:12.015 --> 23:14.810
Miss Chae, if you don't fully understand,
that's how that leech works.

23:14.893 --> 23:17.229
Once he's set foot in the KMA,

23:17.312 --> 23:19.523
he'll invent something that's newsworthy.

23:19.606 --> 23:20.732
So watch out.

23:21.441 --> 23:23.360
It's your territory at the end of the day.

23:23.443 --> 23:26.571
So if he steals a story from under you,
you know what happens, right?

23:26.655 --> 23:27.489
Yeah.

23:27.572 --> 23:29.282
Think about how he'll attack
your co-workers.

23:29.366 --> 23:31.993
- Now, do what you have to do.
- Okay, okay, I got it.

23:35.914 --> 23:38.417
Oh. Hello, I'm from Munmin Daily.

23:38.500 --> 23:39.960
Wow. You're busy.

23:42.129 --> 23:45.549
At the moment, we're unsure
of where the stationary front went.

23:45.632 --> 23:47.801
The North Pacific's anticyclone
is expanding,

23:47.884 --> 23:51.346
so all the hot humid air
is occupying the Korean peninsula.

23:51.430 --> 23:53.515
As long as it does,
the heat will continue,

23:53.598 --> 23:57.686
and the warm nights, meaning
over 25 degrees, will stay as well.

23:59.604 --> 24:01.690
Oh, boy. And if the warm nights
stick around,

24:01.773 --> 24:03.150
electricity use will go up.

24:03.233 --> 24:05.986
And then we'll have
to prepare for blackouts.

24:06.862 --> 24:09.072
Also, we know that the press
will influence the public.

24:09.156 --> 24:11.199
They'll make everyone panic saying,

24:11.283 --> 24:12.951
"It's a sauna."

24:13.034 --> 24:14.995
Or "The deadliest heat wave
of the century."

24:15.078 --> 24:16.746
I'd say that makes a bigger issue.

24:19.875 --> 24:22.461
We've thought that might be a problem,
so we distributed

24:22.544 --> 24:23.962
some official guidelines already.

24:24.045 --> 24:26.798
And the Office of the Spokesperson
will do what we can to limit it.

24:28.842 --> 24:29.718
Okay.

24:30.760 --> 24:31.595
Hm?

24:38.351 --> 24:40.437
Sir, is there a problem?

24:40.520 --> 24:41.480
Oh, no.

24:51.781 --> 24:53.700
That brings us to the end
of today's meeting.

24:53.783 --> 24:55.285
Okay. Great job, everyone.

24:55.368 --> 24:57.746
- Thank you all.
- Thank you.

25:07.380 --> 25:08.840
Hey, come with me.

25:18.099 --> 25:19.226
What's this?

25:20.310 --> 25:21.520
Should we sit?

25:43.375 --> 25:45.460
If you told me we'd be
having this conversation,

25:45.544 --> 25:47.087
I wouldn't believe you.

25:47.170 --> 25:49.673
I wanna know what it's like to be married.

25:53.635 --> 25:54.636
What?

25:54.719 --> 25:57.222
- You're asking me? Seriously?
- Yes, I am.

25:57.806 --> 25:59.641
It's just 'cause I genuinely want to know.

26:00.684 --> 26:01.726
Why?

26:02.352 --> 26:03.770
Lee Si-woo asked you?

26:05.146 --> 26:06.398
I shouldn't have asked.

26:06.481 --> 26:08.775
Ah, okay, okay.
I'll give you a real answer.

26:10.777 --> 26:13.613
What is it like, really?

26:14.614 --> 26:19.369
It's hard to define it as just… as either…

26:19.953 --> 26:21.621
worth it or not. You know what I'm saying?

26:23.039 --> 26:24.207
I know.

26:25.083 --> 26:29.796
Well, it's… you go in thinking that all
you need is for each person to be happy,

26:29.879 --> 26:31.673
but it's more complicated,
that's not true.

26:31.756 --> 26:35.969
There are million other things
that come into play.

26:36.052 --> 26:38.763
And you think there'll be twice
as much drama for the two of us.

26:38.847 --> 26:41.224
Though for us, it's ten times more.

26:42.726 --> 26:45.395
And you already know that.

26:45.478 --> 26:48.023
At the very beginning,
things were rough for us.

26:48.773 --> 26:52.444
We both thought we should be happy now,
but we weren't, for some reason.

26:52.944 --> 26:55.989
I felt like a failure. We started
getting upset over the little things.

26:59.075 --> 27:00.827
Also…

27:02.287 --> 27:05.624
Oh, and before we got married,
we could be selfish.

27:06.374 --> 27:09.461
And now, we're considerate

27:09.544 --> 27:12.964
in ways we never thought
we would've guessed before the wedding.

27:13.715 --> 27:17.093
Things changed. Relationships and things
that used to feel so simple,

27:17.177 --> 27:18.637
became really overwhelming.

27:20.513 --> 27:23.266
And for me, it's been interesting

27:23.350 --> 27:25.894
seeing us change and be vulnerable
like we couldn't before.

27:26.478 --> 27:29.898
Accepting those changes
has been a struggle for the two of us.

27:45.246 --> 27:47.791
Is that the guy? The Munmin leech?

27:47.874 --> 27:48.958
Hm?

27:53.713 --> 27:55.256
Why would they send him here?

27:55.340 --> 27:59.928
You can't be so desperate for a story
that you'd give up on morality.

28:04.933 --> 28:06.267
I'm on it.

28:10.689 --> 28:12.357
Can I speak with you?

28:17.237 --> 28:19.698
All right, here we go,
your strawberry smoothie.

28:20.699 --> 28:22.033
You know, I'm busy.

28:22.117 --> 28:23.034
I do.

28:23.118 --> 28:25.286
But I wanted to get our guest a smoothie.

28:25.370 --> 28:28.331
Well, if you really wanted to dazzle me,
you'd get me a drink.

28:29.874 --> 28:30.709
Mm.

28:32.127 --> 28:34.546
I heard you got married.
You got that glow.

28:34.629 --> 28:35.922
I do?

28:36.005 --> 28:38.800
And the lucky guy,
he works for the KMA, too?

28:39.467 --> 28:40.635
Mm, yeah.

28:43.847 --> 28:46.099
Oh, so you must know all the secrets here.

28:46.182 --> 28:48.643
I wanna know any rumors going around.

28:48.727 --> 28:53.356
Or maybe there's, hm, a power struggle
going on within the KMA.

28:53.440 --> 28:57.152
Or some kind of discrimination?
Any kind of misconduct.

28:57.235 --> 28:59.863
People wanna know
what their officials do all day.

29:01.030 --> 29:03.032
That's why I want to talk to you.

29:03.116 --> 29:04.159
Go on.

29:04.951 --> 29:09.372
Recently, there's a very
high-level conflict that's on-going.

29:09.456 --> 29:10.915
Okay. Who? Details.

29:10.999 --> 29:13.001
I wanna know everything.

29:13.585 --> 29:15.336
High-level, we've got…

29:16.212 --> 29:17.964
General Director Bong-chan…

29:18.047 --> 29:19.716
No, higher.

29:19.799 --> 29:21.176
Way higher,

29:22.218 --> 29:24.721
mT and mP.

29:25.805 --> 29:29.058
mT, mP?

29:34.939 --> 29:35.899
Boo!

29:35.982 --> 29:37.108
You're scared?

29:38.526 --> 29:39.611
Oh, it's Yu-jin.

29:40.111 --> 29:41.613
- Isn't that…
- Huh?

29:41.696 --> 29:43.114
Mr. Heo Ju-yeong from Munmin Daily?

29:43.782 --> 29:45.074
Who's that?

29:45.158 --> 29:47.535
The Butcher 'cause his articles
cut people down.

29:48.661 --> 29:51.164
You know wherever he shows up,

29:51.247 --> 29:53.625
someone's probably gonna lose
their job from his story.

29:53.708 --> 29:56.044
I just don't know
why he'd come to the KMA.

29:56.127 --> 29:58.254
Why is she acting like his best friend?

30:09.682 --> 30:12.352
…mT? m…

30:12.435 --> 30:13.436
Who are they?

30:14.437 --> 30:16.564
They're code names, huh? Tell me.

30:18.817 --> 30:22.946
mT is the Pacific Northern air mass.

30:23.029 --> 30:24.989
mP is the Okhotsk Sea air mass.

30:26.241 --> 30:30.078
The only power struggle that matters here
is the air masses this season.

30:32.330 --> 30:35.917
If you didn't know that, I'm not sure
you're qualified to write about us.

30:40.046 --> 30:41.840
I guess you could still hang out, though?

30:41.923 --> 30:44.759
Um…

30:45.552 --> 30:46.761
So you're saying…

30:47.303 --> 30:51.099
I'm on your territory
and I should piss off?

30:51.683 --> 30:53.142
I'm saying that

30:53.226 --> 30:55.979
if a wonderful reporter like you
covers the smaller stories as well,

30:56.062 --> 30:58.565
new reporters will have a harder time.

30:58.648 --> 31:00.149
It's just the truth, you do it, too.

31:01.359 --> 31:03.361
Uh, if I refuse?

31:03.444 --> 31:07.198
I'd report on a writer whose ethics
are below journalistic standards.

31:07.866 --> 31:10.535
I'd rather be harassed
for shaking the order of things

31:11.119 --> 31:14.581
than stand here and watch you
invent what should be my story.

31:14.664 --> 31:16.207
Somebody is growing up.

31:16.875 --> 31:18.918
Coming from you, that's a compliment.
Thank you.

31:34.058 --> 31:36.644
Some piece of crap.

31:37.312 --> 31:38.938
- They'll let anyone be a reporter--
- Oh!

31:39.022 --> 31:40.023
Uh…

31:41.316 --> 31:42.567
Are you okay?

31:43.359 --> 31:44.402
I'm okay.

31:48.156 --> 31:49.032
Yu-jin.

31:51.117 --> 31:52.911
Can I talk to you for a second?

31:58.333 --> 32:00.209
Time really does fly.

32:00.293 --> 32:02.879
Yesterday, I swear I needed
my winter jacket.

32:03.546 --> 32:04.714
It does.

32:05.715 --> 32:09.093
It's been a million years
since my wedding day.

32:13.097 --> 32:14.265
What can I do for you?

32:18.811 --> 32:19.812
Um…

32:21.272 --> 32:22.941
When I told you

32:23.900 --> 32:26.402
that I never wanted to marry anybody,

32:27.153 --> 32:28.696
what did you think?

32:33.952 --> 32:35.536
Hmm…

32:37.538 --> 32:38.831
In one word, I was…

32:40.083 --> 32:41.042
dumbfounded.

32:42.794 --> 32:44.087
"What's his problem?"

32:44.170 --> 32:46.005
"Why didn't he tell me sooner?"

32:47.256 --> 32:49.884
At first, I was freaking out, absolutely.

32:51.427 --> 32:52.428
And then?

32:54.764 --> 32:56.641
I thought I could change your mind,

32:56.724 --> 32:59.519
then I realized I shouldn't have
to convince you.

32:59.602 --> 33:01.479
And I realized we just…

33:01.562 --> 33:04.190
we wanted totally different things,
that's all.

33:06.317 --> 33:10.238
So I knew there was no way
we could have it worked.

33:19.539 --> 33:21.708
After I figured out that

33:23.668 --> 33:26.337
we would have to call it off one day,

33:28.089 --> 33:30.466
I fell out of love with you,
though it took a while.

33:33.720 --> 33:35.680
Then suddenly, I met Ki-jun.

34:02.165 --> 34:03.666
After I figured out that

34:04.250 --> 34:06.878
we would have to call it off one day,

34:08.254 --> 34:10.757
I fell out of love with you,
though it took a while.

34:24.020 --> 34:26.230
Huh? Huh?

34:26.314 --> 34:28.191
What's with the temperature in Yeouido?

34:31.360 --> 34:33.571
Uh, is there a problem with it?

34:33.654 --> 34:36.074
The website says it's 36.7 degrees.

34:36.157 --> 34:39.202
That means it's somewhat 7 degrees
hotter than any of the areas next to it.

34:39.285 --> 34:40.995
Is it? Is it? Did anyone do the MQC?

34:42.205 --> 34:43.873
Oh, I did sign off earlier.

34:45.333 --> 34:47.210
Did you look at it? This is wrong.

34:47.835 --> 34:49.295
Uh, hang on. Give me a sec.

34:50.004 --> 34:52.632
Take it down, now. Put a blank
on the weather portal if you have to.

34:52.715 --> 34:55.968
- We can't cause more confusion.
- Yeah, I'm doing that.

34:56.052 --> 34:58.638
- Oh, no, that's…
- Here, let me help.

35:16.155 --> 35:18.116
Huh? There's no way.

35:26.207 --> 35:27.750
Hm? Is there a mistake?

35:29.001 --> 35:31.838
Yeouido's high. The temperature is wrong.

35:32.338 --> 35:33.756
Just a typo, I guess.

35:34.340 --> 35:35.383
Typo?

35:39.554 --> 35:40.596
Show me.

35:50.064 --> 35:51.065
Hey.

35:53.442 --> 35:54.402
Uh…

35:55.069 --> 35:57.029
Is Mrs. Oh gonna be okay?

35:57.530 --> 36:00.908
An error on MQC
is a pretty serious sign of negligence.

36:00.992 --> 36:03.703
They'll reprimand her according to policy.

36:03.786 --> 36:06.581
But they know everyone messes up.

36:10.960 --> 36:14.130
- The things you say amaze me sometimes.
- Huh?

36:14.213 --> 36:15.882
We're public officials.

36:15.965 --> 36:17.925
We're not allowed to mess up.

36:26.809 --> 36:28.102
Where are you going?

36:29.187 --> 36:30.479
I need air.

36:35.067 --> 36:36.235
What happens now?

36:36.319 --> 36:38.821
You have to do a write-up
for Mr. Bong-chan?

36:38.905 --> 36:40.615
How long was the error live on the portal?

36:40.698 --> 36:42.116
Less than five minutes, I'd say.

36:44.827 --> 36:47.872
Well, I'll figure it out.
You get back to work, okay?

36:47.955 --> 36:48.915
Okay.

37:05.056 --> 37:06.140
Oh, thanks.

37:10.811 --> 37:13.439
I'm not usually this spacey.

37:13.522 --> 37:14.523
I know.

37:14.607 --> 37:16.192
A mistake like this is unprecedented.

37:16.275 --> 37:17.443
I'm sorry.

37:18.277 --> 37:21.072
I haven't had a good night's sleep
in a couple of days or so.

37:21.656 --> 37:24.742
I don't know, I shouldn't make excuses.
It's unforgivable.

37:26.285 --> 37:27.328
I'm so sorry.

37:29.580 --> 37:32.541
I think you should take an hour
and rest in the night-duty room.

37:33.417 --> 37:36.295
- But the error report--
- I can handle it without you.

37:37.546 --> 37:38.589
Thanks for that.

37:43.469 --> 37:45.680
Um, director?

37:47.348 --> 37:50.142
Think before you marry anybody.

37:52.561 --> 37:55.523
I know you might not wanna hear it,
maybe it's not my place to say.

37:56.315 --> 37:58.818
But when I heard
you called off the wedding,

37:59.402 --> 38:01.112
I felt really proud of you.

38:03.447 --> 38:05.658
I was almost jealous, honestly.

38:05.741 --> 38:08.744
Because once you're married
and you have kids,

38:08.828 --> 38:11.289
'cause that's what you do,
not 'cause you really wanted…

38:12.915 --> 38:15.126
And then there's no way out.

38:17.795 --> 38:21.007
You're a free woman.
You deserve to get anything you want.

38:22.591 --> 38:24.427
Right now, you can do anything
you want to.

38:25.720 --> 38:28.389
Even if it's just enjoying time
to yourself.

38:37.732 --> 38:40.234
If you're ready,
let's go in, follow me.

38:40.318 --> 38:41.527
Okay.

38:48.117 --> 38:49.118
Hello?

38:49.201 --> 38:51.412
Hey, is Bo-mi at school today?

38:54.749 --> 38:56.500
She has a field trip today.

38:57.168 --> 38:58.502
Why? Is she okay?

38:58.586 --> 38:59.962
I just saw her. Bo-mi.

39:00.546 --> 39:02.381
- You what?
- She's at the KMA.

39:02.465 --> 39:04.091
Okay, talk later.

39:08.888 --> 39:10.181
What was that?

39:19.523 --> 39:22.026
You should have called me
and said you'd be here.

39:22.109 --> 39:23.444
I could pull some strings,

39:23.527 --> 39:26.072
so you and your friends
can see the cool stuff behind the scenes.

39:26.155 --> 39:27.615
You're a public official.

39:28.282 --> 39:30.368
You wouldn't abuse public resources,
would you?

39:32.036 --> 39:34.997
Of course not. You're right.

39:35.081 --> 39:37.166
So, now, what have you seen?
Where did you go?

39:37.249 --> 39:39.001
The room for Forecasting and Earthquakes.

39:39.085 --> 39:40.169
Oh.

39:40.753 --> 39:41.921
What do you think of it all?

39:42.004 --> 39:45.216
You can see how hard
we work every day, right?

39:46.759 --> 39:48.094
I've already seen that.

39:48.177 --> 39:49.136
Huh?

39:49.220 --> 39:50.721
Mom always says

39:52.014 --> 39:53.682
that only smart people really know

39:53.766 --> 39:55.309
how hard forecasters work.

39:56.685 --> 39:57.895
I guess.

39:57.978 --> 40:00.856
That's right. So you're smart,
'cause you knew.

40:00.940 --> 40:02.149
That's how it works, right?

40:06.612 --> 40:08.531
Are you coming back another day?

40:08.614 --> 40:11.283
One more day, next week. Why?

40:12.535 --> 40:15.287
I think you need to try
the food in the cafeteria. It's good.

40:15.371 --> 40:16.705
We'll have lunch together.

40:16.789 --> 40:18.207
Just call me when you're here.

40:18.290 --> 40:21.293
Unless that would be abuse
of public resources.

40:22.670 --> 40:24.922
Well, I'll think about it.

40:25.840 --> 40:26.799
Okay.

40:27.466 --> 40:30.553
Think about it. You would have fun.

40:36.308 --> 40:38.144
Why did you want to go there, anyway?

40:38.227 --> 40:40.312
I told you. I went for school.

40:40.396 --> 40:42.398
There were other trips. Why the KMA?

40:42.481 --> 40:45.234
My teacher told me
to get into the high school I like.

40:45.317 --> 40:48.821
I need more science-focused activities,
so I thought I'd go.

40:48.904 --> 40:50.948
You could have at least told me about it.

40:51.031 --> 40:53.117
If I did, you would've said I couldn't go.

40:53.200 --> 40:54.034
What?

40:54.118 --> 40:55.661
You always say the same thing.

40:55.744 --> 40:58.998
You won't even call when it's important,
'cause we can't disturb his work.

40:59.081 --> 41:00.916
And you're sad doing everything alone.

41:01.000 --> 41:02.710
I wanted to see it myself.

41:04.712 --> 41:06.464
What exactly did you want to see?

41:06.547 --> 41:08.424
I want to know what Dad does at work.

41:08.507 --> 41:11.177
Is it really so important
that he had to abandon us?

41:11.260 --> 41:13.179
Why can't he find more time?

41:14.305 --> 41:15.806
Don't I deserve to know that?

41:18.976 --> 41:20.811
So what did you learn
while you were there?

41:20.895 --> 41:23.564
- It was the first day. I don't know.
- So you're going another day?

41:23.647 --> 41:25.107
Sometime next week.

41:38.913 --> 41:40.539
You're sure in a good mood today.

41:41.582 --> 41:42.625
Well…

41:42.708 --> 41:46.879
My daughter visited,
there was a field trip to the KMA.

41:49.590 --> 41:51.800
I realized something interesting.

41:52.510 --> 41:53.761
She actually…

41:54.678 --> 41:56.305
looks like me, a little.

41:58.224 --> 42:00.684
That's not interesting.
It's normal, you know?

42:00.768 --> 42:03.103
I guess it is, huh?

42:03.187 --> 42:06.774
I can't get over how weird it is
having a kid.

42:07.650 --> 42:09.652
I feel like I don't understand her at all.

42:10.236 --> 42:12.363
Somehow. I don't know why.

42:12.446 --> 42:14.782
She still makes me laugh like no one else.

42:15.908 --> 42:17.785
- Oh.
- You're walking on clouds.

42:18.702 --> 42:20.871
Wait until you get married
and have a family.

42:20.955 --> 42:23.040
I can't find the right words
to explain it.

42:23.123 --> 42:25.918
You think you know? You can't.
Not until you're doing it.

42:26.001 --> 42:28.379
Okay, coming from the guy that left home.

42:28.963 --> 42:30.673
You still feel that,
even though it hurt you?

42:30.756 --> 42:33.133
Of course, family is everything.

42:34.635 --> 42:37.888
Si-woo, you shouldn't set aside family
for some adventure.

42:37.972 --> 42:38.806
Like what I did.

42:38.889 --> 42:41.183
Do everything you can to stick together.

42:41.267 --> 42:43.519
You'll always regret
staying away too long.

42:44.687 --> 42:46.730
It's just not worth it.

42:46.814 --> 42:48.774
'Cause… Hold on. Oh.

42:50.359 --> 42:52.319
Stop by
when you're done with work.

42:52.403 --> 42:53.529
Oh, speaking of.

42:53.612 --> 42:54.989
My wife.

42:55.781 --> 42:57.783
- Oh, uh… Yeah.
- Okay.

42:57.866 --> 42:59.410
- Go without me.
- Okay.

42:59.493 --> 43:02.413
- I should go… Go home.
- Yeah, good luck.

43:02.496 --> 43:04.331
- Thanks. Okay.
- Okay.

43:05.207 --> 43:06.709
- Have a good night.
- Okay.

43:12.339 --> 43:13.173
Hello, how are you?

43:13.257 --> 43:15.467
Uh, what do you want?

43:16.719 --> 43:19.138
- This is for you. Here.
- Oh, what is this?

43:19.221 --> 43:20.389
Kimchi.

43:20.973 --> 43:24.893
My mom made it as a way to say thank you
for holding the sides a while ago.

43:24.977 --> 43:26.270
Oh, that's not necessary.

43:26.353 --> 43:29.064
Sorry, is there any way

43:29.148 --> 43:31.817
I could come in
and wash my hands real quick?

43:31.900 --> 43:33.861
Oh, it must have leaked
when I carried it up.

43:34.862 --> 43:36.989
Oh. My hands smell like kimchi, I think.

43:37.072 --> 43:38.198
- Do they?
- I'm sure they're…

43:38.282 --> 43:39.825
- Thanks.
- Wait a minute.

43:40.492 --> 43:42.703
Hang on. Wait a sec.

43:42.786 --> 43:43.746
Ah!

43:53.213 --> 43:54.423
Doors opening.

44:01.055 --> 44:03.349
Oh, what are you doing there, ma'am?

44:03.432 --> 44:04.933
Huh? Oh…

44:05.434 --> 44:07.186
Uh, I was, uh…

44:09.188 --> 44:10.147
You wanna go in?

44:10.230 --> 44:13.692
Oh, I'm okay. Oh, hey, here.

44:14.818 --> 44:18.238
You should take these to the apartment.

44:19.114 --> 44:21.909
You came all the way here with food.
Please, I insist.

44:21.992 --> 44:23.243
I could…

44:25.454 --> 44:26.914
I'll go for a second.

44:26.997 --> 44:28.457
Good.

44:42.429 --> 44:44.306
What are you doing here, Mom?

44:45.140 --> 44:46.934
There are no rules
I can't visit my daughter.

44:47.017 --> 44:48.519
Maybe check your fridge.

44:48.602 --> 44:49.853
Is that enough?

44:54.108 --> 44:56.110
You have to let me know
if you're gonna visit.

44:56.193 --> 44:57.695
- You're making my teammates uncomfortable.
- If that's true,

44:57.778 --> 44:59.613
I'm coming every single day now.

44:59.697 --> 45:01.865
They should be uncomfortable
living with you.

45:04.993 --> 45:06.412
I can handle it. Don't worry.

45:06.495 --> 45:08.580
One day, you'll be married
with a stubborn daughter.

45:08.664 --> 45:10.582
You'll understand why I'm worried then.

45:11.375 --> 45:13.794
Till then, don't get too comfortable.

45:13.877 --> 45:16.422
Senior Um will be back soon.
You should leave before then.

45:16.505 --> 45:18.674
I wouldn't dream of staying here
another second,

45:18.757 --> 45:21.552
- even if you beg me on your knees.
- Oh, here.

45:21.635 --> 45:23.512
I got this for you.

45:24.263 --> 45:25.305
Huh?

45:25.389 --> 45:27.391
- Well, thank you, young man.
- Sure.

45:28.142 --> 45:30.644
Oh, why is she taking so long up there?

45:32.312 --> 45:33.439
She? Who?

45:37.818 --> 45:38.861
Ah…

45:40.446 --> 45:43.991
No, I said… I said that…

45:50.831 --> 45:51.749
Here.

45:51.832 --> 45:54.251
Oh, thank you, sir.

46:00.758 --> 46:02.217
Oh!

46:03.802 --> 46:06.054
You must read a book every day.

46:06.138 --> 46:09.475
It's… No, they're just copies
of the classics.

46:09.558 --> 46:10.768
And he's smartass.

46:10.851 --> 46:12.102
Huh?

46:12.186 --> 46:14.146
Oh, wonderful collection.

46:14.730 --> 46:15.647
Yeah.

46:18.400 --> 46:22.196
You really didn't need to do
any of this for me.

46:22.780 --> 46:26.366
In my family, we never let
a favor go unreturned.

46:26.450 --> 46:28.911
And everyone could use a side dish or two.

46:28.994 --> 46:30.746
What, you eat only dewdrops?

46:30.829 --> 46:32.372
I prefer to cook my own food.

46:33.499 --> 46:35.125
You're particular, aren't you?

46:35.709 --> 46:37.419
Are you an only child?

46:37.503 --> 46:39.630
- Yeah, that's right.
- Mm-hm? Where are you from?

46:39.713 --> 46:41.256
Suwon. Why are you asking me?

46:41.340 --> 46:43.133
I'm curious. I wanted to know.

46:43.217 --> 46:44.718
You work with my sister, I hear.

46:44.802 --> 46:47.179
Yeah, well, that's true.

46:47.262 --> 46:49.765
Tell your mother I'm so grateful and--

46:49.848 --> 46:52.601
You're in the same team
and live in the same place.

46:52.684 --> 46:56.355
Wow. That seems like a sign of something,
it's like destiny.

46:56.438 --> 47:00.275
A lot of our co-workers live
in the building just around this area.

47:01.109 --> 47:03.487
There are six other people working
for the KMA

47:03.570 --> 47:04.822
living in the building.
There could be more.

47:04.905 --> 47:07.115
Oh, it's so convenient.

47:24.424 --> 47:27.386
CITY CROCODILE
BY JIN TAE-KYUNG

47:34.184 --> 47:35.269
Um…

47:36.186 --> 47:39.106
The research was rather lacking,

47:39.189 --> 47:42.276
that's that,
the story was pretty good, so…

47:46.488 --> 47:47.948
What parts did you like?

47:56.874 --> 47:58.000
What?

47:58.083 --> 48:00.127
Tae-kyung is spying on my co-worker?

48:00.210 --> 48:01.837
Listen. It's not--

48:01.920 --> 48:03.714
- Mom! What's wrong with you?
- Don't scream.

48:04.339 --> 48:05.883
We've been over this.

48:05.966 --> 48:08.635
Shin Seok-ho is my subordinate at work.

48:08.719 --> 48:11.179
It's annoying for me.
But how do you think it makes him feel?

48:11.263 --> 48:12.806
How can I look at him at work?

48:14.182 --> 48:15.851
If you need a project,
something to work on,

48:15.934 --> 48:17.436
go fix up your own life!

48:18.770 --> 48:21.523
You're… You're just being cruel now.

48:21.607 --> 48:23.317
I'm your mom. You can't say that.

48:23.400 --> 48:26.278
You have no idea what it's like to lose
sleep worrying about your daughter.

48:26.987 --> 48:28.405
Everything I do is for you.

48:28.488 --> 48:30.157
And you tell me, what?

48:30.240 --> 48:31.450
"Mom, fix your own life"?

48:32.826 --> 48:34.119
It's not right.

48:36.872 --> 48:39.625
Hear that? Even your guest
thinks you're wrong.

48:41.084 --> 48:42.461
Oh, no, I…

48:42.544 --> 48:45.672
I meant you, ma'am. Not Miss Jin.

48:46.965 --> 48:48.008
Huh?

48:48.091 --> 48:50.302
It's clear that when parents force things
on their children,

48:50.385 --> 48:51.970
even if they say it will be good,

48:52.054 --> 48:54.431
the children never actually end up happy
or whatever it is.

48:55.766 --> 48:57.851
Hold on, hold on.
Hang on. You're saying

48:57.935 --> 49:00.437
I should just sit around all day
and watch my own flesh and blood

49:00.520 --> 49:01.563
turn into a spinster?

49:02.189 --> 49:04.232
Waste away, turn down the good men?

49:04.316 --> 49:06.276
Lose the best years of her life for what?

49:06.360 --> 49:10.113
It doesn't really matter if she does,
what matters is if she wants to.

49:10.864 --> 49:14.284
You don't know, you're too young.
You're nearly a child.

49:14.368 --> 49:16.912
- You'll learn one day, marriage--
- It's never happening.

49:18.455 --> 49:19.623
What?

49:23.043 --> 49:25.087
Never am I getting married, Mom.

49:29.716 --> 49:33.095
Oh, no. It's… It's too late.

49:33.178 --> 49:35.597
You need to sleep. We'll talk later.

49:36.181 --> 49:37.182
I mean it.

49:38.517 --> 49:40.560
That's how it is, so you can move on.

49:42.354 --> 49:44.064
No, come on, Ha-kyung.

49:45.273 --> 49:49.403
There's no reason to make a silly decision
out of stubbornness.

49:49.486 --> 49:52.072
Okay, I'll admit.
Your mom went too far today.

49:52.155 --> 49:54.366
It's my fault. I'm sorry. My bad.

49:55.158 --> 49:56.368
I made up my mind, Mom.

49:57.536 --> 50:00.789
You're gonna have a daughter
that's single forever, that's it.

50:00.872 --> 50:03.709
Starting now, no more talk about marriage,
no blind dates,

50:03.792 --> 50:05.252
no more talk about romance.

50:06.169 --> 50:07.004
Ha-kyung.

50:07.087 --> 50:09.423
I need space tonight.
You can see yourself out.

50:10.757 --> 50:11.675
Ah…

50:28.316 --> 50:31.236
That's why they evolved
to have only four toes at the back.

50:32.154 --> 50:33.155
Oh.

50:34.197 --> 50:36.283
You could be a real animal scientist.

50:36.783 --> 50:38.577
Oh, no, I'm no zoologist.

50:39.161 --> 50:40.871
You know enough to be one.

50:40.954 --> 50:43.415
You know so much about animals.

50:45.500 --> 50:47.169
Well, anyone can do that.

50:47.252 --> 50:49.838
I just like them,
so I read about them a lot.

50:49.921 --> 50:51.840
Oh, that's cool.

50:52.340 --> 50:55.177
Oh. What about penguins?

50:55.260 --> 50:57.220
You don't know about penguins, do you?

50:57.971 --> 50:58.930
Penguins?

50:59.431 --> 51:03.101
I thought, for my next book, it might be

51:03.185 --> 51:04.895
about this penguin who does things.

51:06.271 --> 51:08.940
So any penguin facts
would be really helpful for me.

51:09.941 --> 51:13.403
Well, I… I'd say my favorite animal
are penguins, so, yeah.

51:13.487 --> 51:15.614
What? Seriously?

51:15.697 --> 51:18.533
That's amazing!

51:19.159 --> 51:20.786
Could you help me with the pictures, then?

51:23.497 --> 51:24.372
Yeah?

51:25.207 --> 51:27.167
I guess I could.

51:28.752 --> 51:30.253
You have to tell her.

51:30.921 --> 51:31.922
What?

51:32.422 --> 51:35.008
I want you to tell her yourself right now.

51:35.092 --> 51:36.927
What do you want me to tell her?

51:37.010 --> 51:40.263
That she can't visit the KMA
for the field trip to see you.

51:40.347 --> 51:41.890
You're too busy, right?

51:43.850 --> 51:46.853
I'll find time for her.
It's really not a problem.

51:47.854 --> 51:50.899
It's not like it was my idea.
The whole thing was set up by the school.

51:51.817 --> 51:54.236
I'm happy to see Bo-mi at my work.

51:55.195 --> 51:56.113
I'm not, though.

51:57.614 --> 52:00.408
I'm not comfortable with the two of you
at the KMA.

52:00.992 --> 52:02.285
With your co-workers.

52:33.483 --> 52:34.943
What are you doing here?

52:35.443 --> 52:37.988
I'll call a taxi for you.
It's too hot to walk.

52:41.741 --> 52:42.951
It didn't use to get

52:43.577 --> 52:46.830
this hot even in the middle of summer,
it didn't.

52:47.873 --> 52:51.376
I think the weather is learning
from how people are these days.

52:51.459 --> 52:53.211
Huh, 'cause they have to be.

52:54.588 --> 52:58.300
I think it's incredible
that everyone goes on in this heat.

52:59.009 --> 53:01.094
You agree, then. Everyone is tough now.

53:01.178 --> 53:03.722
You don't think it's the other way around,
where people react

53:03.805 --> 53:04.848
to the world they're in?

53:06.600 --> 53:07.642
Was I too tough?

53:07.726 --> 53:09.853
No. That's not what I meant.

53:11.521 --> 53:12.689
Stick to the weather, kid.

53:12.772 --> 53:15.150
I wish I could.
That'd be a dream come true for me.

53:16.526 --> 53:18.486
I don't understand these kids.

53:20.071 --> 53:24.201
Ma'am, you don't have to worry
about Director Jin too much.

53:24.284 --> 53:25.702
She was probably just angry.

53:25.785 --> 53:28.330
She can change her mind.
It's too big of a decision

53:28.413 --> 53:31.458
to just make a choice
and stick to it one day.

53:35.003 --> 53:37.797
Ha-kyung doesn't say things
without certainty.

53:39.341 --> 53:42.427
If she said something,
she really means it.

53:45.805 --> 53:48.225
I was too hard on her, wasn't I?

54:24.552 --> 54:25.804
I got her a taxi.

54:32.686 --> 54:34.521
My mom's a lot, isn't she?

54:34.604 --> 54:36.273
Mm…

54:38.483 --> 54:39.317
Well, she…

54:41.319 --> 54:42.821
cares about everything.

54:44.614 --> 54:46.533
That's every mother and her kid.

54:47.117 --> 54:49.911
If that's true, why did you lie to her?

54:49.995 --> 54:51.204
Lie what?

54:52.497 --> 54:53.707
About getting married.

54:54.833 --> 54:58.003
I've heard that saying
"You won't" really shocks people.

54:58.086 --> 55:00.130
You shouldn't do that as a joke.

55:00.839 --> 55:02.090
I was serious.

55:04.843 --> 55:07.137
Well, serious and that I'm considering it.

55:07.846 --> 55:11.474
Like you said, if people are just waiting
to get married or not, it's suffocating.

55:11.558 --> 55:14.728
I don't want a relationship
where we're bringing each other down.

55:24.195 --> 55:26.656
I'm tired. Let's go to bed.

56:35.558 --> 56:38.645
Due to the influence of the hot and humid
North Pacific's anticyclone,

56:38.728 --> 56:41.356
temperatures during the day
will rise up to 32 degrees nationwide.

56:41.439 --> 56:43.650
And we'll continue to have warm nights.

56:43.733 --> 56:47.570
Our concern is that citizens
are going increasingly fatigued,

56:47.654 --> 56:49.447
purposely caused by the evening heat.

56:49.531 --> 56:52.117
We'll start to see an increase
in workplace and driving accidents.

56:52.200 --> 56:53.410
If you turn to the chart…

56:57.372 --> 56:58.998
The Head Director wants to see you, sir.

57:01.000 --> 57:02.001
You know why?

57:02.710 --> 57:04.337
We're having a meeting. Why?

57:19.060 --> 57:20.270
Director Jin.

57:21.020 --> 57:23.314
Was there an error posted

57:23.398 --> 57:25.316
on the disaster prevention portal
yesterday?

57:30.113 --> 57:31.448
Yes, very briefly.

57:31.948 --> 57:33.992
We corrected the information right away.

57:40.623 --> 57:42.459
When were you gonna tell me that?

57:43.168 --> 57:45.920
You should have submitted a report
to me right away!

57:47.589 --> 57:50.175
We're already called
the "Korean Bullshit Administration."

57:50.258 --> 57:52.051
The "KBA!", "Incompetent!"

57:53.928 --> 57:55.722
This seems like evidence!

57:55.805 --> 57:58.057
MUNMIN DAILY
INCORRECT INFORMATION ON PORTAL SITE

58:01.561 --> 58:02.896
Jesus.

58:04.355 --> 58:07.650
- Where is the Head Director?
- He's in his office right now.

58:07.734 --> 58:08.776
Wonderful.

58:10.111 --> 58:11.154
Good morning, sir.

58:12.113 --> 58:13.281
Yes, of course.

58:14.199 --> 58:15.366
Can I see the tablet?

58:19.704 --> 58:21.789
THE FREQUENT MISREPORTS
WERE PREDICTABLE

58:23.374 --> 58:26.044
Oh, no, damn it. They see it.

58:39.974 --> 58:42.977
Are all reporters totally insane?

58:43.561 --> 58:45.688
It should be illegal
to write stuff like this!

58:46.272 --> 58:47.649
We're only human.

58:47.732 --> 58:49.901
It's almost always accurate. Just a few…

58:52.779 --> 58:54.447
Just one mistake.

58:54.531 --> 58:56.324
They must be bored if they're nitpicking.

58:59.827 --> 59:00.703
Oh.

59:04.541 --> 59:06.918
Someone's probably gonna lose
their job from his story.

59:07.001 --> 59:09.045
I just don't know
why he'd come to the KMA.

59:09.128 --> 59:11.130
Why is she acting like his best friend?

59:14.759 --> 59:17.345
Hey. I didn't miss it.

59:17.428 --> 59:19.430
I chose not to report,
'cause it's nothing.

59:20.807 --> 59:22.684
I know.

59:23.268 --> 59:25.478
It was a small mistake.
It's not worth the page.

59:25.562 --> 59:27.605
And the forecasters
are taking it really hard.

59:28.189 --> 59:29.732
Yes. Okay.

59:31.734 --> 59:34.779
Thanks for hearing my side.

59:35.488 --> 59:36.447
Okay.

59:37.907 --> 59:39.075
Good bye.

59:49.794 --> 59:51.212
We need to talk.

01:00:03.975 --> 01:00:05.059
How is it up there?

01:00:06.185 --> 01:00:08.521
The error
on the disaster prevention portal,

01:00:08.605 --> 01:00:10.064
you tipped him off, didn't you?

01:00:10.857 --> 01:00:11.941
No, I wouldn't.

01:00:12.025 --> 01:00:13.359
I saw it happened.

01:00:13.443 --> 01:00:16.404
I saw you whispering with him
in the cafeteria, with Mr. Heo.

01:00:16.487 --> 01:00:17.697
No, I told you.

01:00:17.780 --> 01:00:19.240
You're trying to deny it?

01:00:20.366 --> 01:00:21.993
You've seen how hard everyone works here.

01:00:22.076 --> 01:00:23.369
You know what we do.

01:00:23.453 --> 01:00:25.246
You just had to help
that guy get a story, huh?

01:00:25.330 --> 01:00:26.372
It's a small error.

01:00:26.456 --> 01:00:28.082
What, you never made a mistake?

01:00:30.793 --> 01:00:32.086
Oppa, you…

01:00:33.129 --> 01:00:35.298
You don't want to listen at all, do you?

01:00:35.381 --> 01:00:36.549
Why should I listen?

01:00:37.050 --> 01:00:38.885
You're not saying anything believable.

01:00:42.388 --> 01:00:44.098
You really don't trust your wife?

01:00:44.932 --> 01:00:46.100
What?

01:00:46.184 --> 01:00:48.144
How can you marry someone you can't trust?

01:00:48.227 --> 01:00:49.854
You don't even trust me enough
to hear me out.

01:00:49.937 --> 01:00:51.272
So how did this happen, huh?

01:00:51.356 --> 01:00:54.525
Yu-jin, what are you saying?
I'm just talking about the article.

01:00:54.609 --> 01:00:56.235
I wanna know what you did.

01:00:56.319 --> 01:00:58.988
And I wanna know why you married
someone you won't hear out.

01:01:00.531 --> 01:01:02.408
'Cause this doesn't just happen
when we're at work.

01:01:02.492 --> 01:01:04.327
Your trust issues are massive.

01:01:04.410 --> 01:01:07.330
Oppa, how can you think
your wife is so awful?

01:01:09.123 --> 01:01:10.249
I wanna know.

01:01:15.838 --> 01:01:17.006
Director Jin.

01:01:17.840 --> 01:01:19.967
Can you manage your team,
or is it too intense?

01:01:20.968 --> 01:01:21.969
I'm sorry, sir.

01:01:22.053 --> 01:01:25.223
'Cause this isn't the first time.
How do we fix things?

01:01:25.306 --> 01:01:27.475
Every day, there's something,
even if it's small.

01:01:28.476 --> 01:01:31.813
Will you be able to make it
through the season?

01:01:31.896 --> 01:01:33.815
With things how they are now.

01:01:35.775 --> 01:01:37.402
I need to know if you can't.

01:01:37.485 --> 01:01:40.029
'Cause I need to do some hiring
if it's too much for you.

01:01:40.113 --> 01:01:41.864
I can do it. I've got it, sir.

01:01:41.948 --> 01:01:45.660
The typhoons haven't even started yet,
and when they do, teamwork's important.

01:01:47.286 --> 01:01:48.621
Don't forget that.

01:01:49.539 --> 01:01:51.332
Yes, sir. I won't.

01:01:51.416 --> 01:01:52.709
Go on.

01:01:53.418 --> 01:01:55.253
Oh, and who are you sending to Jeju?

01:01:55.878 --> 01:01:56.838
What?

01:01:56.921 --> 01:01:59.841
We'll have a typhoon soon.
We need a direct report.

01:01:59.924 --> 01:02:01.884
You need to send someone from your team.

01:02:01.968 --> 01:02:04.929
- You haven't picked?
- Uh, not yet.

01:02:19.110 --> 01:02:20.027
Oh…

01:02:25.116 --> 01:02:26.117
So…

01:02:27.410 --> 01:02:29.287
I have to go. Please forgive me.

01:02:30.413 --> 01:02:33.374
It's… I need to go and get my kids.

01:02:34.417 --> 01:02:36.669
Oh, that's fine. It's fine. Go.

01:02:36.753 --> 01:02:38.004
Yes, um, Miss Kim?

01:02:38.087 --> 01:02:42.216
If you could debrief with Mr. Cho
when he gets in,

01:02:42.300 --> 01:02:44.260
tell him I'll call
and give him more details.

01:02:44.343 --> 01:02:46.053
Okay. I got it.

01:02:46.929 --> 01:02:48.306
Thank you.

01:02:57.064 --> 01:02:59.066
The director is in there being yelled at,

01:02:59.776 --> 01:03:01.861
and she heads out.

01:03:02.445 --> 01:03:04.322
She was the one that signed off
from the air

01:03:04.405 --> 01:03:06.908
but Director Jin chose not to report it
to the General Director.

01:03:12.538 --> 01:03:14.040
Where's Mrs. Oh?

01:03:15.166 --> 01:03:16.417
She had to go get her kids.

01:03:17.585 --> 01:03:20.254
Oh, I told her it was fine
to go get her kids.

01:03:22.089 --> 01:03:24.050
Oh, it is that time, I guess.

01:03:24.634 --> 01:03:26.135
So why don't we all head home?

01:03:26.219 --> 01:03:27.345
- Sure.
- Yeah.

01:03:47.532 --> 01:03:49.575
Don't delay. You make your choice,
and tell them right away.

01:03:49.659 --> 01:03:52.119
They're gonna be out there
for at least a month or two.

01:04:47.216 --> 01:04:48.384
Penny for your thoughts?

01:04:49.427 --> 01:04:50.428
Hm?

01:04:51.012 --> 01:04:52.138
I don't have any.

01:04:52.221 --> 01:04:54.390
Well, you seemed off
ever since you came back

01:04:54.473 --> 01:04:56.517
from the General Director's office.

01:04:56.601 --> 01:04:58.936
Oh, it's the typhoon center.

01:05:00.688 --> 01:05:02.648
Since the typhoons will be starting soon,

01:05:02.732 --> 01:05:05.818
I have to send someone from the team
to Jeju Island.

01:05:05.902 --> 01:05:07.278
Oh.

01:05:14.785 --> 01:05:15.786
Could you do it?

01:05:20.166 --> 01:05:21.584
I'd like it if you'd go.

01:05:39.685 --> 01:05:41.270
We need some time apart.

01:05:44.565 --> 01:05:46.484
What are… What's this about?

01:05:49.278 --> 01:05:50.655
We both need space.

01:05:52.448 --> 01:05:54.450
I think it's important for both of us.

01:05:55.701 --> 01:05:56.619
Yu-jin.

01:05:56.702 --> 01:06:01.248
We should take some time to think
how we can make this work.

01:06:03.209 --> 01:06:05.586
You know you need it as much as I do.

01:06:16.013 --> 01:06:17.306
Are you kidding me?

01:06:18.474 --> 01:06:20.726
All decisions I make at work
are taken seriously.

01:06:26.524 --> 01:06:27.900
So that means…

01:06:28.818 --> 01:06:30.987
you've given this considerable thought.

01:06:32.947 --> 01:06:35.574
Mm-hm. If it's all right with you.

01:06:47.753 --> 01:06:49.005
Is this about

01:06:49.714 --> 01:06:51.632
what you were saying earlier today?

01:06:52.299 --> 01:06:55.136
I think anyone else would have
assumed the same thing.

01:06:55.219 --> 01:06:56.929
Even you, if you were in my shoes.

01:06:57.013 --> 01:06:58.264
No way.

01:06:58.347 --> 01:07:00.683
I would have wanted to hear
what you had to say.

01:07:03.686 --> 01:07:04.937
So, you're saying…

01:07:05.604 --> 01:07:07.440
you're going to leave me right now?

01:07:07.523 --> 01:07:09.233
I just need some space to breathe.

01:07:09.316 --> 01:07:11.527
Every time I see you frown
when you're at home,

01:07:11.610 --> 01:07:13.320
I think it's my fault.

01:07:13.404 --> 01:07:15.031
And I don't deserve to feel like that.

01:07:15.865 --> 01:07:17.783
When have I ever said you make me unhappy?

01:07:17.867 --> 01:07:20.828
Well, you do, in small ways,
like you don't wanna listen.

01:07:22.246 --> 01:07:25.416
It's exhausting to live with someone
that doesn't understand you.

01:07:26.333 --> 01:07:28.461
And you do?
Do you even understand me at all?

01:07:30.004 --> 01:07:33.507
Don't you know how much I love you?
I left the woman I dated for a decade.

01:07:33.591 --> 01:07:36.052
Can you stop saying how you abandoned
someone after ten years?

01:07:37.636 --> 01:07:39.555
I feel awful about that!

01:07:39.638 --> 01:07:42.141
I don't get how you don't think
I love you after that.

01:07:42.641 --> 01:07:45.144
You don't wanna register our marriage,
you're scared of the future…

01:07:45.227 --> 01:07:46.562
Exactly!

01:07:47.980 --> 01:07:51.150
So I think we should take some time
to figure things out.

01:07:53.402 --> 01:07:55.780
Think of what's best for us
and for each other.

01:08:08.000 --> 01:08:11.170
A blizzard of thoughts
swirls in my head these nights.

01:08:18.135 --> 01:08:20.221
Ha-kyung
doesn't just date anybody,

01:08:20.304 --> 01:08:22.098
unless there's a chance of marriage.

01:08:22.181 --> 01:08:23.933
You are aware of that, right?

01:08:24.517 --> 01:08:26.227
If you don't wind up getting married,

01:08:26.310 --> 01:08:30.856
how do you know when you've reached
the height of your love?

01:08:37.863 --> 01:08:39.824
When I have
too many thoughts at once,

01:08:39.907 --> 01:08:41.909
my heart gets confused.

01:08:42.785 --> 01:08:46.872
And a confused heart can only bring more

01:08:48.165 --> 01:08:52.586
and more and more thoughts.

01:09:29.039 --> 01:09:31.458
In our sleepless, too,
warm nights go on.

01:09:31.542 --> 01:09:33.669
The thoughts keep swirling.

01:10:03.866 --> 01:10:05.242
If you leave me right now,

01:10:05.326 --> 01:10:06.744
it's really over between us.

01:10:06.827 --> 01:10:08.454
Are you sure you've thought this through?

01:10:08.537 --> 01:10:10.706
- Who's going to the typhoon center?
- I'm going, sir, it's me.

01:10:10.789 --> 01:10:14.168
I know you want to draw clear lines
between the KMA, me, work, and dating.

01:10:14.251 --> 01:10:17.546
You compare me to him every time,
and it really bothers me.

01:10:17.630 --> 01:10:20.049
I want things
to work out between us.

01:10:20.132 --> 01:10:23.219
Why do you keep confusing me
by changing your stance?

01:10:24.428 --> 01:10:26.055
Someone, please help!

01:10:26.138 --> 01:10:27.890
A student collapsed over here!

01:10:27.973 --> 01:10:29.683
What? An accident?

01:10:30.559 --> 01:10:31.894
Lee Si-woo.

01:10:31.977 --> 01:10:33.479
He works at the KMA.
